  {
   "kind": "text",
   "id": "textTurn_exploreDataFromNL_1792309054970_1792309177736",
   "displayId": "textTurn_exploreDataFromNL_1792309054970_closing",
   "textKind": "explain",
   "content": "**China is catching up, but the US still leads in research.**\n\n| Measure | China | US |\n|---|---:|---:|\n| Research spending, 2023 | **2.58% of GDP** | **3.45% of GDP** |\n| Researchers per million people, 2022 | **1,849** | **4,937** |\n\nChina's research spending, as a share of GDP, rose from **34% of the US level in 2000 to 75% in 2023**. Its researchers per million people rose from 15% to 37% of the US level. Source: UIS, February 2026 release.",
   "parentNodeId": "d_out_6",
   "actionId": "exploreDataFromNL_1792309054970",
